{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.QBetaSpectralBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.QBetaSpectralBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.q_beta_spectral_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.q_beta_spectral_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L297-L331","doc":"**A BARE PROJECTION — this theorem derives nothing.**  Its conclusion\n`Q_beta_A = Q_beta_B` is *character-for-character* the class field\n`forms_agree`, so it restates its own hypothesis.\n\n**Disclosure added 2026-09-04** per bean `qou-pqmw` (78 bare projections,\ntracked with triage pending; this is the entry at this file).  The\nprevious docstring defended the projection as *\"Derived from the class\nfield `forms_agree` — not a `sorry`-projection of an unrelated\nconclusion.\"*  That answers the wrong objection, as\n[`2026-08-09-inhabitation-is-a-weak-discriminator.md`](../../../docs/audits/2026-08-09-inhabitation-is-a-weak-discriminator.md)\n§\"Two shapes worth singling out\" sets out: the §3b-cond item-5 complaint\nis not that the conclusion is *unrelated* to the field but that it is\n**identical** to it.  That audit adjudicated this declaration `genuine`\nin `docs/audits/lean-vacuity-review-ledger.json`.\n\n**What is and is not the defect here.**  The class above is honest —\ncontent-bearing, and uninhabited, which per §3b-tax is the correct state\nfor an open conjecture.  Only this wrapper is the defect, and it is a\ndisclosure defect rather than a mathematical one: nothing false is\nasserted, but a reader scanning for `[inst : …]`-conditional results\nwould count this as one.\n\n**The file's real content is elsewhere and is unconditional:**\n`q_beta_spectral_bridge` above proves the polynomial bridge identity, the\nleading-order ratio identity, and the first-order remainder — with no\nclass hypothesis at all.  Cite that, not this.\n\nClosing the wrapper properly needs the class to relate `Q_beta_A` and\n`Q_beta_B` to the file's `(h, z)` forms, so that agreement *derives*\nsomething — exact agreement would force `z = 1` via the ratio identity.\nThat changes what the block claims and is an authorial call, not a\ncleanup; it is left open rather than guessed at. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.forms_agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.forms_agree","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L294-L294","doc":"**The conjecture itself** (spectral bridge): the two presentations\nof the free-neutron Q-value coincide — Form A equals Form B. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.Q_beta_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.Q_beta_B","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L291-L291","doc":"Form B of the Q-value (transfer-matrix eigenfunction basis),\n`prop:beta-decay-transfer-matrix`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.Q_beta_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.Q_beta_A","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L288-L288","doc":"Form A of the Q-value (NF-counit basis), `prop:neutron-qvalue-symbolic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.mk","kind":"ctor","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L286-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.QBetaSpectral.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark","kind":"class","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L280-L294","doc":"§3b-cond conjecture class for `conj:borromean-quark` as used by the\nQ_β spectral bridge.  Carries the conjectural categorical *inputs*\n(the two presentations of the free-neutron Q-value and the bridge\nidentity relating them) as hypotheses — NOT the conclusion, which is\nderived below per AGENTS.md §3b-cond item 5.  `sorry` in any concrete\ninstance is understood as conjecture per §3b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.q_beta_spectral_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.q_beta_spectral_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L249-L271","doc":"**Q_β spectral bridge — algebraic core.** Combines the three\npolynomial identities into the canonical export. The full\nanalytic statement (with the `Real.log` Taylor remainder)\nfollows from `log_one_add_taylor_bound` once that lemma is\nclosed; see `q-beta-spectral-bridge.md` for the proof outline. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-beta-spectral-bridge","label":"prop:q-beta-spectral-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_taylor_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_taylor_bound","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L235-L238","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_taylor_bound_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_taylor_bound_axiom","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L213-L233","doc":"**External axiom (standard analysis): cubic log Taylor bound.**\n`|log(1+zh) − (zh − (zh)²/2)| ≤ (zh)³` for `0 ≤ zh < 1`.\nPending verification of `Real.abs_log_sub_add_sum_range_le` chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_taylor_bound_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_taylor_bound_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L179-L198","doc":"**Taylor bound on Form B (quadratic-form, fully provable once\nthe lower-bound lemma above lands).** Combines the upper-side\n`log_one_add_upper_taylor_bound` (≤ x²/2) and the lower-side\n`log_one_add_lower_taylor_bound` (≥ 0) into:\n\n  `|log(1+x) - (x - x²/2)| ≤ x²/2`.\n\nThe literature's tighter `x³/3` Cauchy / Leibniz bound is\nsharper, but `x²/2` is **already sufficient** to make the\nbridge identity `Q_β^A = Q_β^B · (1 + (z-1)h/2 + O(h²))` of\n`prop:q-beta-spectral-bridge` rigorous, since the bridge\nstatement only requires an `O(h²)` remainder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_lower_taylor_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_lower_taylor_bound","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L173-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_lower_taylor_bound_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_lower_taylor_bound_axiom","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L152-L170","doc":"**External axiom (standard analysis): log Taylor lower bound.**\n`x − x²/2 ≤ log(1+x)` for `x ≥ 0`, provable via\n`Real.add_one_le_exp + Real.log_le_log` once the chain of Mathlib\nlemmas is verified. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_upper_taylor_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.log_one_add_upper_taylor_bound","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L130-L141","doc":"**Half-bound (upper side, fully proved).** For `0 ≤ x < 1`,\nMathlib's `Real.log_one_add_le_self` gives `log(1+x) ≤ x`. The\nupper side of the Taylor bound follows by subtraction:\n\n  `log(1+x) - (x - x²/2) ≤ x²/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.bridge_first_order_remainder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.bridge_first_order_remainder","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L93-L106","doc":"**Bridge first-order expansion.** Direct algebra shows\n\n  `(1 - h/2) / (1 - z h / 2) - (1 + (z - 1) h / 2)`\n\nequals a quadratic-in-`h` correction divided by `1 - z h / 2`.\nExplicit form: the numerator equals\n`(z (z - 1) - 1 + 1) h² / 4 = (z² - z) h² / 4 = z(z-1) h² / 4`,\nmatching the `O(h²)` Taylor remainder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.leading_order_ratio_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.leading_order_ratio_identity","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L79-L90","doc":"**Leading-order ratio identity.** Multiplying through by the\ncommon factor `h` (assumed non-zero), the Form A / Form B Taylor\nratio reduces to a quotient of linear polynomials in `h`:\n\n  `(h - h²/2) / ((z h - z²h²/2) / z) = (1 - h/2) / (1 - z h / 2)`\n\nNo analysis required — pure field algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.polynomial_bridge_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.polynomial_bridge_identity","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L65-L76","doc":"**Polynomial bridge identity.** The Form A numerator and the\n`z`-rescaled Form B Taylor-truncated numerator share the same\nleading factor of `h`:\n\n  `(h (2 - h) / 2) · z = (1 - h / 2) · (z h)`\n\nThis is the algebraic content of the bridge — the ratio of the\ntwo sides factors `h` cleanly, and the leading-order coefficient\nmatches `1/z + (z-1) h / (2 z)` after dividing through. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.transferLogRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.transferLogRatio","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L46-L52","doc":"Form B's numerator (algebraic leading-order form):\n`ln(1 + z h)`. At single wrap this equals `ln(V_pp / V_nn)` to\n`O(h²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.deltaNetMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.deltaNetMagnitude","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L41-L44","doc":"Form A's numerator: the NF-counit factor `|Δ(net)| = |h (2 - h) / 2|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.heckeH","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L38-L39","doc":"The Hecke–Skein quantum-integer differential `h(q) = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.markovZ","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-beta-spectral-bridge.lean#L33-L36","doc":"The Markov–Jones parameter `z(q) = 1 / (√q + 1/√q)` controls\nthe conversion between the NF-counit basis and the transfer-\nmatrix eigenfunction basis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}